WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.630
Currently, your memory pattern

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.210
is 1, 3, 5, 4 and 2.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.670
even though it should have been

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:17.790
1 2 3 4 5.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.750
Alan, listen to me.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.170
You have a problem with memorization.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.000
Maybe you had left that room,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.170
but you just couldn't remember?

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.500
I don't want to be here anymore.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.710
Please get me out of this place.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.130
But me must plan carefully.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.420
I'm not dreaming, am I?

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.960
Can we travel to somewhere
near Rangsit Khlong 12?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.290
I have a friend named Nate.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.830
Are you sure your friend won't send us back to the hospital?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.790
Jealous?

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:35.580
I dunno.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.880
I just don't want anyone else
to matter more to you than I do.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:38.630
Alan.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:39.830
Run, hurry!

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:40.880
Found him!

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:36.630
Once upon a time, a man

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.630
had a dream he was a floating butterfly.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.750
When the butterfly became weary,

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:43.210
it landed on the branch and fell asleep.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.830
When the butterfly slept,

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:46.539
the man woke up.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.500
When the man fell back asleep again,

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.000
the butterfly awakened.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.630
When the butterfly went to sleep,

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.920
the man awoke.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.750
The man'd slept,

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.210
the butterfly awoke.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.500
Over and over.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:52.540
Win.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.829
Win.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:12.500
Win.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.130
Mister.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.710
Oh, Alan.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.540
Who are you?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.130
Alan.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.130
I'm your dad.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.209
Dad?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.000
Dad.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:27.750
Dad.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:30.960
Dad.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.250
Alan!

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.210
Alan!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.670
Dad.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.290
I tried talking to him, but
he hadn't yet spoken much.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:09.000
He seems different.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.670
Did you do anything?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.250
I increased his
medication dosage.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.790
What medicine, Doctor?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.500
This has been too
much for him already.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.630
It was the same medication,
but at a higher dose.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.750
It was also the best method

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.290
for controlling his behavior.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.000
If we hadn't done this,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.170
he wouldn't have calmed
down and cooperated.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.670
And about his hospital escape,

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.290
how did he manage to get out?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.170
He might have escaped
through the cemetery.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.380
Why did he escape?

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.580
He's never escaped before.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.170
Doctor Nil.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.040
Should we try changing
the treatment method?

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.290
Change?

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.830
How would you change that?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.580
Isn't what we've been
doing right now our best?

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:11.540
I believe that if
we keep doing this,

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.170
he will definitely be treated..

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.790
Listen to me, Doc.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.380
I think this method may no
longer be effective with him.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.290
He just forgot who I was today.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.170
I don't want to leave him
here like this anymore.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.380
If this keeps happening,

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.960
I'll come take him
home next week.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.920
I...

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.920
You asked me to look after him,

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.750
but you never had
any faith in me?

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.170
I did.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.250
I always trusted you.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.330
But maybe we've
reached the dead-end.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.040
Are you a doctor, huh?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.250
Are you a doctor to state
that this is a dead end?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.580
Are you a doctor with the
authority to judge me like that?

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.630
We've been in this
situation for too long.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.750
Don't you ever get tired?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.380
I love him so much, Doctor.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.040
I want him to get better.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.830
But if things like
this continue,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.670
I will not stand it anymore.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.210
You think I didn't love him, Alex?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.960
I love him as much as you do.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.000
And if I were you,

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.290
I would never let my loved
ones become like that forever.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.080
Nevertheless,

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.000
I'll remain true to what I said.

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:48.790
Sorry Nil,

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.460
if I hurted your feelings.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.210
You are free to do as you please.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.750
My duty is over, so if you'd excuse me.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:34.210
O.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.330
Nil.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.250
What are you doing all alone in here?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.000
I

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.580
I need a little change of scenery.

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:02.790
Sometimes being in the same corner

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:05.380
stresses me out.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.000
I've got some things to think about.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:17.420
Did you

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.040
have an argument with Alex in the morning?

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.330
Do you think doctors

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:29.750
are allowed to be discouraged?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.500
Do you think we need to be able to handle

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.540
every situation?

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.960
Do we have to put up with
whatever everyone throws at us?

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.000
Doctors are human too.

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.540
It's normal for us to be tired.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:45.710
Right?

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.830
What's your opinion on Alan's case?

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:02.790
What about that?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.790
Do you believe we can treat him?

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.210
We definitely going to make him better.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.330
Everything all right?

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.250
I think I may have to

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.580
find someone else

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.580
to take over my responsibilities.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:26.330
Nil.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.420
We have come too far

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:30.130
to give up at this point..

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.880
I didn't mean I was
going to stop treating him.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.500
I just feel like I'm not ready.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.000
I'm having trouble managing
several things at once right now

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.790
so I may need to take a break before

00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:45.630
I'm capable of resuming my duties as a doctor.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.210
Would you look after Alan's case for me?

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:01.330
You can't just throw your work at me like that.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:03.880
I've thought it through.

00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:05.960
What if he doesn't approve of me?

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.500
You're closer to him than I am.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.380
You've been with me and Alan

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.040
for long enough.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.000
I believe you can do it.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.420
What choices do I have?

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.170
Thank you.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.500
I really mean it.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.040
Don't make such a sad face,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.540
you'll get me even more worried.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:41.920
Alright?

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.540
Go for it.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.170
My memory

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.540
has started to return

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.000
every time I read this journal.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:55.380
Although I can't remember
exactly what happened that day,

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.830
the sensation has never faded.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:00.790
I have a profound feeling

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.710
and I miss him very much.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.630
But I'm starting to have a harder
time recognizing Win's face.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.290
How many days have passed

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.130
since Win and I haven't met?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.130
Did something happen to him

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.830
after the incident that day?

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:32.210
It's time for your medication, Alan.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:43.500
Please take the pills.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.540
When you're finished,

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.880
please open your mouth.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:06.920
Is it really necessary to open my mouth?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.790
Just making sure, Alan.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.080
Sure about what?

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:13.420
Alan.

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.540
I'm just doing my job.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.080
Who gave the order?

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:18.920
Was it Doctor Nil?

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.330
It was my order.

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:31.000
What gives you the authority to order me?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.750
It's my authority as your
case's personal doctor.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.290
My case's personal doctor?

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:46.080
What about Doctor Nil?

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:48.920
At this time,

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.170
Doctor Nil has his hands full of cases,

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.500
so I took this opportunity to

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.460
take over and handle your case in his place.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:57.880
Personally,

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.290
I believe we're quite close.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.500
This wouldn't be a problem for you, is it?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:04.960
So what?

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.380
If I were to have a problem,

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.000
would anyone in this place care about me?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:15.830
Alan.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.170
Try to give it some careful thought.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.830
Have the doctors

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.000
really never cared about you?

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.790
Weren't the doctors,

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.080
all this time,

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.170
the ones who were
trying to understand you?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:35.750
Guess you're right.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.000
I also wanted to let you know that,

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.710
as a doctor,

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.000
my responsibility is to treat you.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:48.250
However, treating a
patient until they're cured

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.250
is not so simple.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:53.170
There are numerous
other factors involved.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:56.130
But do you know

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:58.580
what's the most important?

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.000
What is it?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.540
Try to guess.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.210
Medications?

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:12.330
Surgical procedures?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:13.580
Wrong answers.

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:15.210
Just tell me what
the answer is, Doc.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:18.130
It's the doctor-patient relationship.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.750
Simply put,

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.670
the trust between a doctor and a patient.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.830
Despite how well the treatment is,

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:29.880
if the doctor and the
patient don't trust each other,

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:31.710
that treatment wouldn't work out at all.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.580
We don't need to talk about

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.920
whether you'll get better or not.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.670
And the fact that I told
Pete to keep checking

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:40.790
to see if you had taken
all of your medications

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.040
not that I didn't trust you,

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.130
but I needed to keep records

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.830
in accordance with the treatment plan.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.500
Therefore,

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.710
should we work together

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.960
to help you get better sooner?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.830
If trusting you

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:24.210
means I'll get better sooner,

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.710
then let's go for it.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.250
Thank you

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.210
for having faith in me.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.500
I promise

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:40.330
that I'll do my best.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.210
Okay.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:50.670
Alan.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:52.210
I believe

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.830
you'll certainly be well again.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.829
What are your thoughts on the earlier.

00:17:09.329 --> 00:17:10.670
That was pretty dramatic.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.710
Dramatic?

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.130
I knew you were

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.500
acting to earn the patient's trust.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.579
Which nursing school did you graduate from?

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.960
Any hospital makes use of this technique.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.380
Hey.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.080
Why do you have to be so serious?

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:33.000
I was just fooling around.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:35.380
You had a smart mouth when you were in that room.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.380
Guess whose face looks
so stressed right now.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.630
I'm not stressed.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.330
I'm a doctor,

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.330
so it's normal for me to appear serious

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.880
in order for the patient to trust me.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.130
They called it

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:52.880
the doctor-patient relationship.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:53.920
Got it?

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:56.670
Brilliant words!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.830
And how about the doctor-nurse relationship?

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:01.830
What do you think?

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:06.960
What are you talking about?

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.250
What's the hurry?

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:17.750
What are you doing?

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.710
This is a hospital.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.170
Well, a little birdy told me

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.500
that you like me.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.670
Who told you that?

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:36.250
I'm going to tell you

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:39.920
that I like you too.

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.540
Is it okay to kiss you?

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:03.500
No.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:28.210
Then,

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.920
maybe another time?

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:39.130
How would I know

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.920
you're not lying to me?

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.330
Guess I'll

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.960
have to leave you with this.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.920
I like you, Doctor.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.000
Would you mind if I sit with you?

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:44.380
Sitting alone with your
mind elsewhere like this,

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.380
did I wake you up

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:48.630
from the sweet daydream you were having?

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.710
Would you like a match?

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:07.380
The dark pieces are yours.

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:13.080
Today is the last day that I'll be here.

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:17.170
I'd like to play a last match with you

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.790
on my final day in this place.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:20.710
If you win,

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:23.500
you can ask me anything.

00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:26.170
I'll answer you as much as I can.

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:28.830
Are you interested

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:30.170
in this offer?

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:31.290
Where are you going?

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:35.460
I have to go back home.

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:38.880
So be it.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.670
Today, it seems like

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.210
your mind is wandering off.

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:48.670
Perhaps I am going to be the victor.

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:53.750
Do I

00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:55.630
look distracted?

00:22:58.130 --> 00:22:59.630
Yeah, you look strange.

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:00.880
I don't know.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.290
I can sense that.

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:08.580
So

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:10.460
Win is not coming?

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:12.920
Win?

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:22.170
Alan!

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:23.710
Run, hurry!

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:28.000
I haven't seen
him for a while now.

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:29.710
Oh dear.

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:32.040
I thought the two of you were inseperable.

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:34.000
Did you guys fight or something?

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:36.580
No.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:40.630
It's kinda strange though.

00:23:42.750 --> 00:23:44.920
I didn't feel like I wanted to see him,

00:23:48.330 --> 00:23:49.880
nor did I even miss him.

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:54.630
Very strange.

00:23:56.960 --> 00:23:59.080
They increased your
medicine dose, haven't they?

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:06.830
Yes.

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:10.080
I see.

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:13.000
That medicine...

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:15.750
what about it?

00:24:18.080 --> 00:24:19.670
Take a good look at yourself.

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:22.130
Since the dosage has been increased,

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:24.630
we're calmer than before.

00:24:25.380 --> 00:24:27.750
That's because doctors here use medications

00:24:27.790 --> 00:24:29.170
to keep the patients under control.

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:32.250
It felt a bit blurry

00:24:32.290 --> 00:24:33.540
obedient,

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:37.250
and perfectly happy, right?

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.710
But you should ask yourself

00:24:46.170 --> 00:24:49.210
if this is actually what you desire.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.830
You seem to have a pretty good grasp of my thoughts.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.040
despite having only known each other for a short time.

00:24:58.790 --> 00:25:02.170
I'm just speaking as someone
who has been here for a long time.

00:25:02.630 --> 00:25:04.000
and has witnessed lots of things.

00:25:04.880 --> 00:25:07.080
Actually, I'm beginning to suspect

00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:10.380
that the treatment in this place
haven't improved my condition at all.

00:25:14.540 --> 00:25:16.080
There were also the medications

00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:19.580
that you said the doctors
increased the dosage of,

00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:22.880
which made me look like a nutcase.

00:25:25.380 --> 00:25:26.380
Maybe

00:25:26.630 --> 00:25:27.630
I was just talking nonsense.

00:25:27.790 --> 00:25:29.540
What were you expecting from the patient...

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:30.330
That's not true.

00:25:30.460 --> 00:25:31.330
...like me?

00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:33.540
If you know something,

00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:34.880
you better tell me.

00:25:36.880 --> 00:25:38.040
I think that

00:25:39.130 --> 00:25:40.460
the two of us

00:25:42.080 --> 00:25:43.960
have something in common.

00:25:48.670 --> 00:25:49.670
How are we alike?

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:51.080
You and I

00:25:51.670 --> 00:25:54.000
have been trying to bridge the gap

00:25:54.710 --> 00:25:56.080
between imagination

00:25:56.130 --> 00:25:57.460
and reality.

00:25:57.960 --> 00:25:59.130
Sometimes,

00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:02.170
what we thought were imaginations

00:26:02.880 --> 00:26:04.460
or dreams

00:26:05.130 --> 00:26:07.710
turned out to be reality.

00:26:08.380 --> 00:26:10.920
However, what we believed to be real

00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:13.580
got muddled and mixed up

00:26:14.080 --> 00:26:15.380
to the point that

00:26:15.790 --> 00:26:17.080
we had no idea what was true.

00:26:20.420 --> 00:26:21.670
Dreams...

00:26:22.130 --> 00:26:23.790
were like hallucinations.

00:26:25.040 --> 00:26:27.080
They might have had some kind of truth

00:26:27.130 --> 00:26:29.380
trying to communicate with us.

00:26:29.710 --> 00:26:32.750
Perhaps it was just a ripped page

00:26:33.670 --> 00:26:36.210
from our memory journal.

00:26:37.380 --> 00:26:40.080
But, no matter how torn apart it was,

00:26:41.210 --> 00:26:43.210
it did contain something

00:26:43.290 --> 00:26:45.580
that could be linked to our past.

00:26:46.130 --> 00:26:47.130
Checkmate!

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:49.290
Darn it.

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:51.790
Even while hazy,

00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:54.170
you still made a comeback.

00:26:56.170 --> 00:26:58.540
I was just following my instincts.

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:01.790
Now.

00:27:03.710 --> 00:27:05.170
Since I've won,

00:27:06.250 --> 00:27:07.580
you have to keep your promise.

00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:09.210
Time for you to answer my question

00:27:09.420 --> 00:27:10.580
like we agreed.

00:27:24.880 --> 00:27:26.040
Who is this man?

00:27:26.830 --> 00:27:27.960
You knew him, right?

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:32.130
Who is this man?

00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:36.080
I really can't

00:27:37.790 --> 00:27:39.000
answer that.

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:40.790
You're lying.

00:27:41.210 --> 00:27:42.290
You promised

00:27:42.630 --> 00:27:44.250
you'd tell me if I won.

00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:49.500
This is all I can help you.

00:27:49.880 --> 00:27:52.130
You have to find the answers on your own, boss.

00:27:53.380 --> 00:27:54.080
That's not true.

00:27:54.130 --> 00:27:55.290
You promised me.

00:27:55.460 --> 00:27:57.210
You told me we were alike.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:27:59.000
If we really are alike

00:27:59.080 --> 00:28:01.040
then you must understand how I feel!

00:28:01.670 --> 00:28:02.420
Please

00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:03.250
I beg you, Si.

00:28:03.330 --> 00:28:04.080
Help me!

00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:05.500
Please help me!

00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:10.000
I've returned something for you under
the table where we first played chess.

00:28:11.670 --> 00:28:14.000
No matter what the outcome was today,

00:28:14.210 --> 00:28:16.670
I intended to give it back to you anyway.

00:28:17.130 --> 00:28:18.290
What is it?

00:28:18.380 --> 00:28:20.000
What is it, tell me?

00:28:21.380 --> 00:28:22.500
Who is this old man?

00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:25.380
Miss Si?

00:28:25.540 --> 00:28:26.670
Where are you?

00:28:26.790 --> 00:28:28.460
Your family is here to take you home.

00:28:45.330 --> 00:28:47.000
No matter how many times

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:48.000
you get haunted,

00:28:48.290 --> 00:28:50.960
I want you to trust your own instincts.

00:28:51.540 --> 00:28:53.920
Trust your own instincts!

00:28:54.670 --> 00:28:56.000
Good luck, chief.

00:29:04.080 --> 00:29:08.000
I've returned something for you under
the table where we first played chess.

00:29:09.790 --> 00:29:12.130
No matter what the outcome was today,

00:29:12.330 --> 00:29:14.920
I intended to give it back to you anyway.

00:29:16.130 --> 00:29:18.540
I've compared both of the journals.

00:29:19.460 --> 00:29:21.000
The handwriting was certainly mine.

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:24.880
There's no denying that the stories were mine.

00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:27.210
This is another notebook in which I wrote,

00:29:27.540 --> 00:29:29.710
but I had written it five months ago.

00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:31.130
What the heck is this?

00:29:31.380 --> 00:29:32.920
Have I been here before?

00:29:33.580 --> 00:29:34.290
6

00:29:34.630 --> 00:29:35.250
7

00:29:35.540 --> 00:29:36.250
8

00:29:36.710 --> 00:29:37.460
9

00:29:42.080 --> 00:29:43.380
Today, I had a treatment session

00:29:43.670 --> 00:29:44.790
with Doctor Nil

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:46.210
and Doctor O.

00:29:48.330 --> 00:29:50.670
Doctor Nil asked me about
the nurse on the other night.

00:29:50.880 --> 00:29:52.790
I've never seen that nurse before.

00:29:52.830 --> 00:29:55.420
Never had memories of her in my head.

00:29:56.290 --> 00:29:58.000
Are you sure

00:29:58.670 --> 00:30:00.880
you have never seen this nurse before?

00:30:02.210 --> 00:30:04.000
One of the patients

00:30:04.130 --> 00:30:06.080
came to greet me in the cafeteria today.

00:30:06.330 --> 00:30:07.380
He was pretty cute

00:30:07.420 --> 00:30:08.750
and friendly.

00:30:09.210 --> 00:30:10.540
He told me his name was Win.

00:30:10.880 --> 00:30:12.580
This is not the first time I'm here.

00:30:13.290 --> 00:30:15.210
I first met Win five months ago.

00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:17.290
Our beginning was the same.

00:30:18.830 --> 00:30:20.000
I didn't like him

00:30:20.790 --> 00:30:22.170
until we opened up,

00:30:23.830 --> 00:30:25.170
spent time together,

00:30:26.880 --> 00:30:27.880
fell in love.

00:30:30.330 --> 00:30:31.330
What the hell?

00:30:31.710 --> 00:30:34.210
My life is a movie that replays back and forth?

00:30:36.960 --> 00:30:37.960
Alan?

00:30:44.380 --> 00:30:45.250
Alan.

00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:47.880
Alan.

00:30:48.380 --> 00:30:49.330
There you are.

00:30:49.580 --> 00:30:50.790
I've been looking
for you everywhere.

00:30:51.210 --> 00:30:52.460
Oh, Pete.

00:30:54.170 --> 00:30:55.250
Do you need anything?

00:30:55.580 --> 00:30:57.040
Time for your medications.

00:30:59.210 --> 00:31:00.000
Alright.

00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:17.380
All done.

00:31:29.380 --> 00:31:30.210
Alan.

00:31:30.580 --> 00:31:31.830
Get plenty of rest

00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:33.170
so you can get well soon.

00:31:34.330 --> 00:31:35.040
Okay.

00:32:49.920 --> 00:32:51.380
Win's room, as I've noted

00:32:51.830 --> 00:32:53.040
is either 303

00:32:53.790 --> 00:32:55.000
or 305.

00:32:55.790 --> 00:32:57.290
I didn't write it down very clearly.

00:33:05.210 --> 00:33:06.000
Win.

00:33:09.130 --> 00:33:10.130
Win.

00:33:18.420 --> 00:33:19.170
Win.

00:33:21.380 --> 00:33:22.250
Win.

00:33:29.170 --> 00:33:30.000
Alan.

00:33:32.330 --> 00:33:33.330
Quick! Get in!

00:34:10.250 --> 00:34:11.130
Alan.

00:34:14.790 --> 00:34:16.210
How did you make it here this far?

00:34:22.630 --> 00:34:24.080
I miss you so much.

00:34:28.170 --> 00:34:29.380
I'm so sorry

00:34:31.830 --> 00:34:33.210
I didn't visit you.

00:34:35.170 --> 00:34:36.170
Since that day,

00:34:37.540 --> 00:34:38.540
I've been scared.

00:34:41.290 --> 00:34:42.960
I didn't want to get you in trouble anymore.

00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:49.500
Win.

00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:55.080
Why...

00:34:57.540 --> 00:34:58.920
did you

00:34:59.790 --> 00:35:01.290
decide to approach me?

00:35:10.580 --> 00:35:12.040
Can you answer me that?

00:35:14.710 --> 00:35:15.580
What?

00:35:17.080 --> 00:35:18.080
I asked you

00:35:19.630 --> 00:35:21.330
why you chose to talk to me

00:35:26.000 --> 00:35:27.920
when there were a lot of other people.

00:35:29.790 --> 00:35:30.630
I...

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.000
I only thought you could be my friend.

00:35:38.710 --> 00:35:39.830
I had been alone for a long time,

00:35:39.830 --> 00:35:40.830
and I felt lonely.

00:35:41.710 --> 00:35:42.710
I wanted to have friends.

00:35:44.330 --> 00:35:45.330
Why?

00:35:45.830 --> 00:35:47.250
Which time are you referring about, Win?

00:35:58.290 --> 00:36:00.000
This notebook

00:36:01.750 --> 00:36:03.670
contains our stories.

00:36:04.630 --> 00:36:06.170
I just got it

00:36:06.330 --> 00:36:07.750
not long ago.

00:36:12.080 --> 00:36:13.210
The inside of this notebook

00:36:13.790 --> 00:36:15.250
is filled with so many stories

00:36:16.830 --> 00:36:18.920
between me and you.

00:36:23.880 --> 00:36:25.130
Shall I read

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:27.460
some of them for you?

00:36:29.210 --> 00:36:30.630
Which one should I pick first?

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:35.000
Let's read this one.

00:36:36.290 --> 00:36:38.750
It was May 5th.

00:36:40.040 --> 00:36:41.540
The sun was scorching hot that day.

00:36:42.830 --> 00:36:44.880
Win took me for a walk in the garden.

00:36:47.290 --> 00:36:48.960
But the sun light was really hot,

00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:50.630
so we hid in the shade.

00:36:51.830 --> 00:36:54.210
On June 15,

00:36:55.790 --> 00:36:57.960
Win was going to take me to the cemetery,

00:36:58.960 --> 00:37:00.080
but I was terrified.

00:37:00.130 --> 00:37:01.250
So Win told me that

00:37:01.920 --> 00:37:03.170
if I no longer felt scared,

00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:05.580
he would take me there again

00:37:07.420 --> 00:37:08.880
on June 5th.

00:37:11.830 --> 00:37:13.210
Win asked me to be his partner.

00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:19.580
What's the meaning of all of this?

00:37:20.920 --> 00:37:21.830
Hmm?

00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:25.960
Would you tell me

00:37:27.630 --> 00:37:30.580
what everything in this notebook is all about?

00:37:31.710 --> 00:37:32.540
Hmm?

00:37:35.830 --> 00:37:36.750
Or

00:37:38.830 --> 00:37:40.540
did you scheme up

00:37:41.750 --> 00:37:43.830
with those doctors to deceive me?

00:37:44.710 --> 00:37:45.710
Huh?

00:37:48.330 --> 00:37:49.580
Answer me, Win!

00:37:50.210 --> 00:37:51.500
Answer me.

00:37:52.750 --> 00:37:54.330
I never wanted to decieve you.

00:38:02.330 --> 00:38:03.460
You know,

00:38:04.210 --> 00:38:05.880
at this point in my life,

00:38:07.500 --> 00:38:09.750
I have lost all my trust in everyone.

00:38:11.920 --> 00:38:12.920
The doctors?

00:38:15.040 --> 00:38:16.630
Or even with you.

00:38:17.960 --> 00:38:19.210
Be honest with me, Win.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:21.250
How does it feel

00:38:22.330 --> 00:38:23.380
to have

00:38:24.420 --> 00:38:26.040
to come see my face

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:29.290
everyday

00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:33.210
and trick me

00:38:34.960 --> 00:38:36.540
every time?

00:38:39.290 --> 00:38:40.210
Hmm?

00:38:41.830 --> 00:38:43.040
I have reasons

00:38:45.670 --> 00:38:47.250
why I had to approach you this way.

00:38:49.170 --> 00:38:50.420
What reasons?

00:38:55.500 --> 00:38:57.710
Because you have a
memory condition, Alan.

00:39:04.460 --> 00:39:07.290
I had to become a stranger in your eyes

00:39:09.250 --> 00:39:10.670
again and again.

00:39:12.630 --> 00:39:14.330
Why didn't you tell me?

00:39:17.250 --> 00:39:18.500
It wasn't easy

00:39:20.380 --> 00:39:23.000
that I had to come to you and
tell you we'd known each other,

00:39:24.460 --> 00:39:25.790
but you couldn't remember.

00:39:29.580 --> 00:39:31.540
I wasn't easy for me at all.

00:39:37.080 --> 00:39:40.420
I'd always be the one
missing from your memory,

00:39:42.960 --> 00:39:45.210
while in my memory,

00:39:46.170 --> 00:39:47.920
you're still in there.

00:39:57.380 --> 00:39:59.170
But I've never blamed you, Alan.

00:40:02.500 --> 00:40:04.000
Because I loved you so much,

00:40:04.420 --> 00:40:06.380
that's why I allowed things to go this way

00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:10.580
no matter how many times they'd happen.

00:40:14.750 --> 00:40:16.790
If I go back to forgetting things again,

00:40:20.500 --> 00:40:22.040
would you come back for me?

00:40:26.920 --> 00:40:28.330
Please don't leave me.

00:40:32.830 --> 00:40:34.080
Please come back for me.

00:40:37.460 --> 00:40:38.460
I promise

00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:46.080
no matter how many times it happens again,

00:40:48.710 --> 00:40:49.960
I'll always come back for you.

00:40:52.630 --> 00:40:53.580
Hey.

00:40:55.670 --> 00:40:57.170
There's a place

00:40:58.330 --> 00:40:59.830
I'd like to go.

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:06.330
In this notebook

00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:08.380
of mine.

00:41:10.330 --> 00:41:12.170
I wrote down multiple stories

00:41:13.290 --> 00:41:14.830
between myself

00:41:15.330 --> 00:41:16.580
and the director's office.

00:41:20.710 --> 00:41:21.880
I noted that

00:41:23.920 --> 00:41:25.670
I had seen the old man ghost

00:41:25.830 --> 00:41:27.500
at the director's office.

00:41:30.460 --> 00:41:31.880
I'm sure you know.

00:41:36.750 --> 00:41:38.130
There must have been some connection

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:40.210
between me and
that room, for sure.

00:41:43.790 --> 00:41:45.880
Would you take me to that room?

00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:48.290
If you want me to trust you again,

00:41:48.960 --> 00:41:50.630
of course.

00:41:54.540 --> 00:41:55.710
Would you, Win?

00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:16.040
Is this here?

00:42:19.880 --> 00:42:21.710
Why is this the only separated building?

00:42:22.710 --> 00:42:23.710
So weird.

00:42:24.830 --> 00:42:27.000
This place was probably
where he spent most of his life.

00:42:30.630 --> 00:42:31.630
Let's take a look inside.

00:43:04.080 --> 00:43:07.960
What do you know about this former director?

00:43:09.580 --> 00:43:12.710
He had intended to utilize this land
as a community for psychiatric patients,

00:43:14.330 --> 00:43:15.630
but that never happened.

00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:19.920
What kind of person was he?

00:43:20.880 --> 00:43:22.000
I only know that

00:43:23.420 --> 00:43:25.000
he had good intentions

00:43:25.170 --> 00:43:26.420
when he built this place.

00:43:29.710 --> 00:43:31.210
Because he had also struggled hard

00:43:32.630 --> 00:43:33.830
since he had nothing.

00:43:36.580 --> 00:43:38.960
From an orphan with no family

00:43:40.500 --> 00:43:42.000
to becoming a psychiatrist

00:43:42.250 --> 00:43:44.000
who had been acknowledged at that era.

00:43:47.290 --> 00:43:48.790
So where is he right now?

00:43:49.580 --> 00:43:50.630
Is he dead?

00:43:55.080 --> 00:43:56.210
No one knows.

00:44:04.170 --> 00:44:05.290
Are you ready?

00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:19.420
I'm right here with you,

00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:23.960
but in the end...

00:44:24.830 --> 00:44:27.000
You're going to have to make
your own decision what to do next.

00:44:28.670 --> 00:44:30.040
But if this is the only way

00:44:31.170 --> 00:44:32.580
that'll get you the answers,

00:44:34.960 --> 00:44:36.290
then there's nothing more to be afraid of.

00:44:59.880 --> 00:45:00.790
What?

00:45:01.130 --> 00:45:03.250
I saw you were stunned and thought you'd been haunted.

00:45:04.250 --> 00:45:05.250
You asshole.

00:45:05.460 --> 00:45:06.670
I almost pissed myself.

00:45:07.080 --> 00:45:08.080
Shit!

00:45:09.830 --> 00:45:10.830
Alan.

00:45:19.830 --> 00:45:20.960
Where are you?

00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:24.000
Where are you?

00:45:24.580 --> 00:45:25.630
Where are you?

00:45:28.710 --> 00:45:29.710
Where are you?

00:45:29.750 --> 00:45:31.040
Get yourself out here!

00:45:41.250 --> 00:45:42.460
Alan.

00:45:51.830 --> 00:45:52.830
Who are you?

00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:54.500
What do you want from me?

00:45:59.330 --> 00:46:00.540
Just answer me!

00:46:02.080 --> 00:46:03.630
Remember.

00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:07.130
If you can't remember, come back to me.

00:46:08.330 --> 00:46:09.330
Return to where?

00:46:10.630 --> 00:46:12.080
Where do you want me to go?

00:46:12.710 --> 00:46:14.080
Where do I have to return to?

00:46:14.380 --> 00:46:15.130
Huh?

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:16.830
Come back to me.

00:46:17.710 --> 00:46:19.080
He's not your father.

00:46:21.000 --> 00:46:22.210
Who's not my father?

00:46:25.080 --> 00:46:26.250
Who's not my father?

00:46:28.420 --> 00:46:29.500
Who's not my father?

00:46:31.960 --> 00:46:33.380
Hey, wait!

00:46:33.380 --> 00:46:34.500
Come back!

00:46:45.290 --> 00:46:46.290
Did you hear?

00:46:46.580 --> 00:46:48.040
Did you hear what he said?

00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:50.920
No.

00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:52.830
What did he say?

00:46:53.500 --> 00:46:54.920
He said my dad

00:46:58.330 --> 00:46:59.630
wasn't my real father.

00:47:30.170 --> 00:47:31.170
Dad?